## 4. Semantics

### 4.1 Value Space

Truth values are **continuous** in the interval \([0, 1]\):

| Value | Interpretation |
|:---|:---|
| \(1\) | Approachable truth (ideal, unattainable limit) |
| \(0\) | Approachable falsehood (ideal, unattainable limit) |
| \(0.5\) | Homogenesis (generative ground) |
| \((0.5, 1)\) | Closer to truth |
| \((0, 0.5)\) | Closer to falsehood |

### 4.2 Valuation Function

Let \(v: \text{WFF} \to [0, 1]\) be a valuation function.

#### Atomic Valuation

\[
v(p) \in [0, 1]
\]

#### Constants

\[
v(\mathcal{H}_g) = 0.5
\]

\[
v(\mathcal{O}_c) = 0.5 + \delta \text{ where } \delta \in (-0.25, 0.25)
\]

#### Classical Connectives

| Connective | Formula |
|:---|:---|
| Negation | \(v(\neg \phi) = 1 - v(\phi)\) |
| Conjunction | \(v(\phi \land \psi) = \min(v(\phi), v(\psi))\) |
| Disjunction | \(v(\phi \lor \psi) = \max(v(\phi), v(\psi))\) |
| Implication | \(v(\phi \to \psi) = \min(1, 1 - v(\phi) + v(\psi))\) |
| Biconditional | \(v(\phi \leftrightarrow \psi) = 1 - |v(\phi) - v(\psi)|\) |

#### Organic Connectives

**Homogenetic Negation (\(\sim\))**

\[
v(\sim \phi) = 
\begin{cases}
1 - v(\phi) & \text{if } v(\phi) \neq 0.5 \\
0.5 & \text{if } v(\phi) = 0.5
\end{cases}
\]

**Interpretation:** When at the middle (homogenesis), negation is stable—it remains at the middle. Otherwise, negation generates the opposite.

**Organic Conjunction (\(\oplus\))**

\[
v(\phi \oplus \psi) = \frac{v(\phi) + v(\psi)}{2} + \alpha \cdot v(\phi) \cdot v(\psi) \cdot (1 - |v(\phi) - v(\psi)|)
\]

Where \(\alpha \in [0, 1]\) is the **integration parameter**.

**Interpretation:** Organic conjunction integrates both conjuncts. When they differ (contradiction), the result is higher than classical conjunction due to productive tension.

**Generative Implication (\(\otimes\))**

\[
v(\phi \otimes \psi) = 
\begin{cases}
\min(1, v(\psi) + \beta \cdot (v(\phi) - 0.5)) & \text{if } v(\phi) \neq v(\psi) \\
0.5 + \gamma \cdot (v(\phi) - 0.5) & \text{if } v(\phi) = v(\psi)
\end{cases}
\]

Where \(\beta, \gamma \in [0, 1]\) are **generativity parameters**.

**Interpretation:** Generative implication produces new form from the tension between antecedent and consequent.

**Organic Disjunction (\(\ovee\))**

\[
v(\phi \ovee \psi) = 1 - v(\neg \phi \oplus \neg \psi)
\]

**Interpretation:** Organic disjunction is the dual of organic conjunction—integrative OR.

#### Acknowledgment Operator

\[
v(A(\phi)) = 
\begin{cases}
1 - |v(\phi) - 0.5| & \text{if } v(\phi) \neq 0.5 \\
1 & \text{if } v(\phi) = 0.5
\end{cases}
\]

**Interpretation:** Acknowledgment is highest when at homogenesis (pure ground) and decreases as we move toward extremes.

